I) in localStorage. If caching, use memory-only storage or implement encryption using TweetNaCl.js or libsodium.js.\",\n    \"Enhance URL validation in isValidUrl(): extract and validate hostname/domain against whitelist. Use new URL() to parse, then verify url.hostname is in allowed domains list.\",\n    \"Implement Content-Security-Policy (CSP) headers on backend: set 'script-src 'self'' to prevent inline script execution, 'style-src 'self'' for stylesheets. Mitigates XSS impact significantly.\",\n    \"Sanitize transcript and user-generated content: use DOMPurify library before rendering. Create <textarea> wrapper component that HTML-escapes by default, only accepts structured transcript objects.\",\n    \"Add runtime config validation: create Zod/Yup schema for RuntimeConfig, validate JSON.parse result against schema. Fail gracefully with clear error if schema validation fails.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Key findings summary:**\n\n1. **Token Storage (HIGH)**: The most critical issue — tokens in localStorage are vulnerable to XSS. This is your biggest attack surface.\n\n2. **CSRF Protection (HIGH)**: State-changing requests lack CSRF tokens, allowing attackers to forge requests from other sites.\n\n3. **401 Handling (HIGH)**: No redirect to login means users experience undefined behavior and potential information leakage.\n\n4. **Error Exposure (MEDIUM)**: Backend errors leaked to frontend could expose system architecture to attackers.\n\n5. **Unencrypted Cache (MEDIUM)**: localStorage-based caching without encryption stores any cached data in plaintext.\n\n**Recommended remediation priority:**\n- Week 1: Migrate to httpOnly cookies + CSRF protection (highest impact)\n- Week 2: Add 401 redirect, sanitize errors, validate API_BASE\n- Week 3: Sanitize user-generated content, enhance URL validation\n- Ongoing: Add CSP headers, secure cache, config validation\n\nWould you like me to implement any of these fixes in the codebase?\n",
